# Room 3 — hidden trading defaults

If a default decides **how much money**, **when orders fire**, **flatten/kill**, or **session gates**, it must be said out loud in UI and in chat. Do not let equal-split sizing, silent 1-share fallbacks, or similar sit until the first fill.

When adding execution logic: put the rule on the execution posture / watch book, and tell the user in plain language.

**Size:** Engine-internal. Trading today is **$0 until you Set $ / tap a %** each session. Next trading day (4:00 AM ET) it zeros again — you set it when you sit down. Same day it stays what you set (reconnect / push must not wipe it). Inside that cash: **75% 15m / 17.5% 5m / 7.5% 1m**; leftover from quiet TFs diverts to whatever is actually printing. The first fire of a TF takes that pot (not 1/N crumbs). Working tickets at $2M: **1m $100k · 5m $200k · 15m $300k**; uncapped letters may take the full slot. Ticket ≤ **7% of that name’s session $vol so far**. This print stays at **5%** so one order does not lift the bar. No volume printed → no ticket. A smaller Set $ uses the same percents. Watch-book Size $ shows that fire-ready amount while warming.

**9:30–10 is open (2026-10-04).** New fills are allowed through the old letter skip windows. 3A noon cut stays.

**S1 shelf (2026-10-06, one-time).** The then-current purgatory pile may fire as **S1 (1M/5M/15M)** — nearest ≥85%, same TF, placeholder Handle. Not bolted onto 2A / 2C / 1B. If an older live letter is also ≥85% on that bar, the older letter keeps the shot. S1 fires when it is the only one. New packs still sit. Local until Cloud push.

**Fire floor (2026-09-21 / fat 2026-09-27):** detect and display stay **≥85%** — that is the gene and every letter lock still reads that way. **Quiet tape fires at ≥88%.** **This-print fat may fire at ≥85%.** Quiet 85–87 still shows "family at N% · fires at ≥88% — watching". TNON is not a veto — Aug 12 / Aug 19 days rose after the nick. A live 15m can add once. **15m fill** waits for a **green last bar** (Handle 2026-09-28); red still matches. **Letter ticket cap** then clips at **$2M working size**: 1m **$100k** · 5m **$200k** · 15m **$300k**. No fire at **$0**: 5m 5C / 5m 3A / 5m 4A / 15m 8B. Uncapped (TF slot may grow, up to 5% of this print): 15m **1A / 2B**, 5m **1A / 8A / 1B / 9A / 2B**, 1m **3G / 3B / 7B**. Scale the Set $ down later — the same percents, a smaller slot. Size $ note shows the cap. Do **not** dump this as a lecture on the operator screen.

**Fat tape (2026-09-22 / fire 2026-09-27):** **this print** **≥4.5%** is Handle, not a new letter. May fire at **≥85%**. Stop **max(8%, this print)**. Hold **~20 min** or until the letter flips — no +20% take. Wick / limit fill of **this print**. First-of-day and cool do not block another shot. Watch book says "fat tape · wait the wick" until the low prints. Not a 5m/15m envelope.

**1m exits (2026-09-27):** letter clip (stop + target). Not pooled **25% / 10%**. 5m stays **8% / 8%**. 15m stays **30% / 10%**. Quiet **15m 2B** (2026-10-02): after **+12%**, trail **10% off the high**. Fat 2B stays the 20-minute box.

**Same day:** Checkboxes gate **new entries**. Post on → open trades may hold through post. Post off → at RTH close: flatten opens, drop committed maps, **clear the belt** (clean slate for the evening). Always flatten by ~8:00 ET. Overnight flat.

**Belt:** Drop **adds** names — they stay through the trading windows you enabled. Max **15**. × removes one; Clear wipes all. Post off at RTH close also clears the belt. Several names can be in at once. One ticker = one open position at a time (Alpaca is one pile of shares). A second 1m letter may add as its own lot. **1m: max 3 fills per name per day** (all letters share the count); after that, no new 1m on that name until the next session.

**Orders:** Price off **Alpaca last**, not Yahoo close. Detect 1m is **Massive** when it answers (same tape as the $2M house), else **Alpaca**, Yahoo last. Style is **per strategy**: pops (scalp/sniper/impulse, and unnamed 1m) → market; slower setups on any TF → limit. Outside RTH always limit. Kill / day-end flatten uses limit.

**Kill:** FLAT disarms, clears belt, drops committed queues, flattens open paper positions, and **stops laptop-closed trading**.

**Laptop closed (Cloud):** Arm + belt starts a process pulse so detect/fire/hold/exit continue after the tab dies. Disarm or Kill stops it. Streamlit Community Cloud can still **sleep the whole app after ~12 hours with no visitors** — a morning open + Arm is enough for a normal session; it is not a forever-on server.
